            <ArticleTitle>Osteoid Osteoma of the Talar Neck With Subacute Presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E404-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoid osteoma of the talar neck is a rare clinical entity that is frequently missed on initial assessment in patients with ankle pain. We present a case report of an adolescent with talar neck osteoid osteoma who presented with persistent pain after an injury. We review the differential diagnosis of persistent anterior ankle pain and review the treatment options for osteoid osteoma of the talar neck.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
